IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`

-- wra-core-tests.l4: a smoke test of wra-core.l4, and a set of construction shapes the part agents can copy.
-- It proves that every record and every enumeration in the core can be built and read back, and that the core imports
-- cleanly with prelude and daydate. It encodes no provision of the Act.
-- The fixtures below are invented people and amounts with no legal content. Where an expected value comes from the
-- Act's text, the comment beside the assertion says which line of inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt it comes from.

§ `Fixtures`

`Asha` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference` IS "asha"
    `age in years` IS 34
    `date of birth` IS Date 12 3 1992
    `where the person is` IS `Greater London`
    `where the person lives` IS `Greater London`

`Ben` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference` IS "ben"
    `age in years` IS 36
    `date of birth` IS Date 2 9 1990
    `where the person is` IS Wales
    `where the person lives` IS Wales

`Caleb, a child` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference` IS "caleb"
    `age in years` IS 3
    `date of birth` IS Date 5 7 2023
    `where the person is` IS `Greater London`
    `where the person lives` IS `Greater London`

-- Raw line 422 (s 39(1)(a)): two people who are married to each other and are members of the same household
`Asha and Ben's relationship` MEANS `Relationship of two people` WITH
    `married to each other or civil partners of each other` IS TRUE
    `members of the same household`                         IS TRUE
    `living together as if married or civil partners`       IS FALSE

`Asha and Ben` MEANS `Two people` WITH
    `the first person`  IS `Asha`
    `the second person` IS `Ben`
    `their relationship` IS `Asha and Ben's relationship`

-- Raw lines 8-9 (s 1(2)): an individual who is not a member of a couple, or members of a couple jointly
`Asha claiming alone` MEANS `a single claimant` `Asha`
`Asha and Ben claiming jointly` MEANS `joint claimants` `Asha and Ben`

`Asha's household` MEANS Household WITH
    `the claimants` IS `Asha claiming alone`
    `the children and young persons` IS LIST `Caleb, a child`

GIVEN claimants IS A Claimants
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many people claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER claimants
    WHEN `a single claimant` person THEN 1
    WHEN `joint claimants` people   THEN 2

GIVEN claimants IS A Claimants
GIVETH A STRING
`the reference of the first claimant` MEANS
    CONSIDER claimants
    WHEN `a single claimant` person THEN person's reference
    WHEN `joint claimants` people   THEN people's `the first person`'s reference

§ `Places, people, couples, households`

#ASSERT `Asha`'s `where the person lives` EQUALS `Greater London`
#ASSERT NOT (`Ben`'s `where the person lives` EQUALS `Greater London`)
#ASSERT `Ben`'s `where the person is` EQUALS Wales
#ASSERT `Asha`'s `date of birth` EQUALS Date 12 3 1992
#ASSERT `Asha and Ben`'s `the second person`'s reference EQUALS "ben"
#ASSERT `Asha and Ben`'s `their relationship`'s `members of the same household`
#ASSERT NOT (`Asha and Ben`'s `their relationship`'s `living together as if married or civil partners`)
#ASSERT `how many people claim` `Asha claiming alone` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `how many people claim` `Asha and Ben claiming jointly` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the reference of the first claimant` `Asha claiming alone` EQUALS "asha"
#ASSERT `the reference of the first claimant` `Asha and Ben claiming jointly` EQUALS "asha"
#ASSERT count (`Asha's household`'s `the children and young persons`) EQUALS 1

§ `Employers and decision-makers`

`an employer` MEANS Employer WITH `the employer's reference` IS "acme"

#ASSERT `an employer`'s `the employer's reference` EQUALS "acme"
#ASSERT `the Secretary of State` EQUALS `the Secretary of State`
#ASSERT NOT (`an authorised person` EQUALS `the Secretary of State`)   -- s 29(1) (raw line 350): an authorised person is someone the Secretary of State authorises
#ASSERT NOT (`a court` EQUALS `the First-tier Tribunal`)

§ `Benefits, periods, awards and payments`

-- Raw line 1343: "the relevant year" means the year beginning with 6 April 2011 (only the first day is stated there)
`the year beginning 6 April 2011` MEANS Period WITH
    `first day` IS Date 6 4 2011
    `last day`  IS Date 5 4 2012

`Asha's universal credit award` MEANS Award WITH
    `the benefit awarded`    IS `universal credit`
    `who it is awarded to`   IS `Asha claiming alone`
    `the period awarded for` IS `the year beginning 6 April 2011`
    `the amount awarded for the period, in pounds` IS 6000

`a hardship payment to Asha` MEANS Payment WITH
    `the kind of payment`       IS `a hardship payment`
    `the benefit paid`          IS `universal credit`
    `the person it was paid to` IS `Asha`
    `the period paid for`       IS `the year beginning 6 April 2011`
    `the amount paid for the period, in pounds` IS 250

#ASSERT `the year beginning 6 April 2011`'s `first day` EQUALS Date 6 4 2011
#ASSERT `Asha's universal credit award`'s `the benefit awarded` EQUALS `universal credit`
#ASSERT `Asha's universal credit award`'s `the amount awarded for the period, in pounds` EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `a hardship payment to Asha`'s `the kind of payment` EQUALS `a hardship payment`
#ASSERT `a hardship payment to Asha`'s `the person it was paid to`'s reference EQUALS "asha"
-- Raw lines 383-384 (s 33(1)(a)-(b)) and 390-391 (s 33(2)): the Act names income-based jobseeker's allowance and income-related employment and support allowance, not the allowances in general
#ASSERT NOT (`income-based jobseeker's allowance` EQUALS `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance`)
#ASSERT NOT (`income-related employment and support allowance` EQUALS `contributory employment and support allowance`)

§ `Work-related requirements and sanctions`

-- s 13(2): four requirements (raw lines 131-135); s 13(3): four groups (raw lines 136-140)
`the four work-related requirements` MEANS LIST `work-focused interview requirement`, `work preparation requirement`, `work search requirement`, `work availability requirement`
`the four groups` MEANS LIST `no work-related requirements`, `work-focused interview requirement only`, `work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only`, `all work-related requirements`
-- Sch 5 para 1(3) (raw lines 3059-3062) names five reductions: s 26, s 27, JSA 6J, JSA 6K and WRA 2007 11J; Sch 6 para 5(4) (raw lines 3163-3167) names more
`the reductions Schedule 5 paragraph 1(3) names` MEANS LIST `universal credit higher-level sanction`, `universal credit other sanction`, `jobseeker's allowance higher-level sanction after universal credit`, `jobseeker's allowance other sanction after universal credit`, `employment and support allowance sanction`

#ASSERT count `the four work-related requirements` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT count `the four groups` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT count `the reductions Schedule 5 paragraph 1(3) names` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT elem `work search requirement` `the four work-related requirements`
#ASSERT NOT (elem `income support sanction` `the reductions Schedule 5 paragraph 1(3) names`)

§ `Personal independence payment`

-- s 77(2): an entitlement may be to the daily living component, the mobility component, or both (raw lines 1348-1351)
`a daily living component at the enhanced rate` MEANS `Entitlement to a component` WITH
    `the component` IS `daily living component`
    `the rate`      IS `enhanced rate`
`a mobility component at the standard rate` MEANS `Entitlement to a component` OF `mobility component`, `standard rate`

#ASSERT `a daily living component at the enhanced rate`'s `the rate` EQUALS `enhanced rate`
#ASSERT `a mobility component at the standard rate`'s `the component` EQUALS `mobility component`
#ASSERT NOT (`standard rate` EQUALS `enhanced rate`)

§ `Decisions, steps after a decision, and recovery`

-- s 97(6) (raw line 1598): a decision to apply the benefit cap
`a benefit cap decision` MEANS Decision WITH
    `the kind of decision`  IS `a decision to apply the benefit cap`
    `the decision-maker`    IS `the Secretary of State`
    `the benefit concerned` IS `universal credit`
    `the date it was made`  IS Date 1 5 2013

#ASSERT `a benefit cap decision`'s `the kind of decision` EQUALS `a decision to apply the benefit cap`
#ASSERT `a benefit cap decision`'s `the decision-maker` EQUALS `the Secretary of State`
#ASSERT `a benefit cap decision`'s `the date it was made` EQUALS Date 1 5 2013
-- s 105 inserting 71ZB(3)(b) (raw line 1688): a determination "revised or superseded under section 9 or section 10"
#ASSERT NOT (`revision` EQUALS `supersession`)
#ASSERT NOT (`appeal to the First-tier Tribunal` EQUALS `appeal to the Upper Tribunal`)
-- s 105 inserting 71ZB(7) (raw lines 1693-1697): four ways to recover
#ASSERT NOT (`deduction from benefit` EQUALS `deduction from earnings`)
#ASSERT NOT (`court action` EQUALS `adjustment of benefit`)
